households, I'd start with a **2,000Wh (2kWh) battery**\\. It's a practical balance between runtime, portability, and cost.\n\n## Top options I found\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn623791product3\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n(Budget pick)\n\n**\ue200entity\ue202[\"turn623791product3\",\"Anker SOLIX C1000 Gen 2 Portable Power Station (1024Wh, 2000\u2026\"]\ue201**\n\n## \\$549.99\n\nB&amp;H Photo \u00b7 1,024Wh \u00b7 2,000W output\n\nGood for short outages, internet, laptops, lighting, and limited refrigerator backup.\n\n\ue200url\ue202View product\ue202https://www.bhphotovideo.com/c/product/1929018-REG/anker_a17631a1_solix_c1000_gen_2.html?BI=23971&kw=ANSLXC1000G2&utm_medium=feed&utm_source=chatgpt.com\ue201\n\n---\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn623791product25\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n(Best value for home essentials)\n\n**\ue200entity\ue202[\"turn623791product25\",\"EcoFlow Delta 3 Max 2400/3400W 2kWh Portable Power Station F\u2026\"]\ue201**\n\n## \\$879.00\n\nHome Depot \u00b7 2,048Wh \u00b7 2,400W output\n\nRoughly twice the battery capacity of a 1kWh unit. Suitable for a refrigerator, Wi-Fi, and several small devices.\n\n\ue200url\ue202View product\ue202https://www.homedepot.com/p/EcoFlow-Delta-3-Max-2400-3400W-2kWh-Portable-Power-Station-For-Home-Backup-Camping-RVs-EFD3M-G-US/336910271?fp=oai&utm_medium=feed&utm_source=chatgpt.com\ue201\n\n---\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn623791product2\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n**\ue200entity\ue202[\"turn623791product2\",\"Anker SOLIX C2000X Gen 2 2,400-Watt/2,048Wh Portable Power S\u2026\"]\ue201**\n\n## \\$969.00\n\nHome Depot \u00b7 2,048Wh \u00b7 2,400W output\n\nAnother strong home-backup option, with expandable capacity for longer outages.\n\n\ue200url\ue202View product\ue202https://www.homedepot.com/p/Anker-SOLIX-C2000X-Gen-2-2-400-Watt-2-048Wh-Portable-Power-Station-Home-Backup-Outdoor-RV-Push-Button-Start-Battery-Generator-A1785/338538419?fp=oai&utm_medium=feed&utm_source=chatgpt.com\ue201\n\n---\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn623791product9\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n**\ue200entity\ue202[\"turn623791product9\",\"Jackery Explorer  2000 v2 Portable Power Station\"]\ue201**\n\n## \\$1,239.00\n\nJackery \u00b7 2,042Wh \u00b7 2,200W output\n\nA relatively lightweight 2kWh alternative. Manufacturer currently indicates preorders shipping November 16.\n\n\ue200url\ue202View product\ue202https://www.jackery.com/products/jackery-explorer-2000-v2-portable-power-station?utm_campaign=openai_catalog&utm_content=product_card&utm_medium=feed&variant=44024634179671&utm_source=chatgpt.com\ue201\n\nPrices are from current shopping listings and can change. Independent testing guides also recommend EcoFlow, Jackery, and Anker for home backup. \ue200cite\ue202turn623791news12\ue202turn623791news13\ue201\n\n## How long will a battery last?\n\nThese are illustrative estimates, assuming 85% usable AC energy after conversion losses.\n\n| Appliance | 1kWh battery | 2kWh battery |\n|--------|--------|--------|\n| Wi-Fi router (15W) | 57 hours | 113 hours |\n| Laptop (60W) | 14 hours | 28 hours |\n| Refrigerator (60W average) | 14 hours | 28 hours |\n| Fan (50W) | 17 hours | 34 hours |\n\nActual runtime varies. Refrigerators cycle on and off and need extra starting power. Air conditioning, electric heaters, and ovens consume much more energy. Never connect a portable power station to household wiring without an approved transfer system installed by a qualified electrician.\n\n## What size do you need?\n\nWhat do you want to power?\n\nPhones, laptops, Wi-Fi\n\nRefrigerator, Wi-Fi, lights\n\nMultiple appliances or home circuits\n\nHow long should it last?\n\n8 hours\n\n24 hours\n\n3 days\n\nBudget\n\nUnder \\$500\n\n\\$500\u2013\\$1,000\n\n\\$1,000\u2013\\$3,000\n\nOver \\$3,000\n\n[Find the best battery for my home]"},{"p":"/message/metadata/model_dil_v2/recoveryDiagnostics","o":"remove"}],"c":14} 

